message.content:
Fluorescein injection is a diagnostic reagent for administration to patients, put up in measured doses. That points to heading 3006, which covers pharmaceutical goods such as "opacifying preparations for X-ray examinations; diagnostic reagents designed to be administered to the patient." The relevant subheading is 3006.30, which covers opacifying preparations for X-ray examinations and diagnostic reagents designed to be administered to the patient. Under 3006.30.10 are the preparations for X-ray, and 3006.30.50 is "Other."

I recall the HTSUS structure as follows: 3006.30.10 covers barium sulfate, 3006.30.50 covers other. I'm not certain of the exact statistical suffixes for 3006.30. I believe the line is 3006.30.1000 for "Opacifying preparations for X-ray examinations; diagnostic reagents designed to be administered to the patient: Barium sulfate" and 3006.30.5000 for the other items. Fluorescein sodium injection is classified in 3006.30.5000.

